# DRAFT: nothing has been released yet. The version, date and DOI are filled in at release.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use NewsAttention, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "NewsAttention: daily news events linked to how many people read about them on Wikipedia"
abstract: >-
  NewsAttention links the dated news events listed on Wikipedia's Current Events Portal to
  daily page views of the articles they link to, by language edition (Wikimedia Analytics API)
  and by country (Wikimedia's differentially private page-view files), with derived measures
  of attention: baseline, lift, peak day, half-life and breadth.
authors:
  - family-names: Kraishan
    given-names: Obada
    affiliation: "College of Media and Communication, Texas Tech University"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/obadaKraishan/newsattention"
keywords:
  - public attention
  - news events
  - Wikipedia page views
  - communication research
  - journalism
  - dataset
